= Scoped rules

#{ $.set({kind: 'heading', level: 2}, {color: '#2f5d8a'}) }

A rule set at the top level styles everything after it: the section heading below is blue.

== Inside a region

#!aside
Before the rule, `code` is plain.

#{ $.set('code', {color: '#a8432a'}) }

After it, `code` is red, to the end of the region.
#aside!

After the region, `code` is plain again.

- one `a`
- two
  #{ $.set('code', {italic: true}) }
  `b` is italic, to the end of the item
- three `c` is not
